<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">14 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 14 June, from 1645 to 1982.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1645 CE <span class="tih-ago">381 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">New Model Army defeats Charles I at Naseby</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fairfax and Cromwell's New Model Army destroyed the main royalist army in Northamptonshire. Captured royal letters damaged the king's cause, and the First Civil War was effectively decided.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1777 CE <span class="tih-ago">249 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress adopts the Stars and Stripes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Flag Resolution called for thirteen stripes, red and white, and thirteen white stars on a blue field. The anniversary is celebrated in the US as Flag Day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1800 CE <span class="tih-ago">226 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon wins at Marengo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near defeat by the Austrians, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> was saved by Desaix's arriving division, and the battle turned. The victory secured northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and his position as First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consul</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consul</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1940 CE <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">German troops enter Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wehrmacht">Wehrmacht</a> marched into the French capital, which had been declared an open city. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> signed an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> eight days later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1982 CE <span class="tih-ago">44 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Argentine forces surrender at Port Stanley</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The surrender ended the 74-day Falklands War, in which 649 Argentine and 255 British service personnel died. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>'s military junta fell soon after.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a></div></div></li></ol>
